---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="kinds-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">// what you're installing</p>
    <h2 id="kinds-title">Two kinds of files</h2>
    <p>
      Both are plain markdown with YAML frontmatter. Claude Code picks them up from your project's
      <code>.claude/</code> folder, or from <code>~/.claude/</code> for every project.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="kinds">
    <article class="kind kind-agent">
      <div class="kind-head">
        <span class="badge badge-agent">sub-agent</span>
        <h3>A specialist Claude can hand work to</h3>
        <p>
          A sub-agent runs in its own context window with its own system prompt and tool allowlist.
          Claude delegates to it when a task matches its description, or when you ask for it by
          name. The result comes back without cluttering your main conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="meta">
        <dt>runs in</dt>
        <dd>A separate context window</dd>
        <dt>triggered</dt>
        <dd>Claude delegates, or you ask: "use the code-reviewer"</dd>
        <dt>best for</dt>
        <dd>Reviews, audits, research, test writing: focused jobs</dd>
      </dl>
      <div class="kind-file">
        <div class="kind-file-path">
          <Icon name="file" />
          .claude/agents/code-reviewer.md
        </div>
        <pre><span class="d">---</span>
<span class="k">name</span>: code-reviewer
<span class="k">description</span>: Reviews code changes for bugs…
<span class="k">tools</span>: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash
<span class="d">---</span>

You are a senior engineer doing a careful review…</pre>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="kind kind-skill">
      <div class="kind-head">
        <span class="badge badge-skill">skill</span>
        <h3>Know-how Claude loads when it's needed</h3>
        <p>
          A skill is a folder of instructions, plus optional scripts and references. Only its
          description sits in context until a task calls for it, then Claude reads the rest and
          follows it in your main conversation. You can also run it directly as <code>/name</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="meta">
        <dt>runs in</dt>
        <dd>Your main conversation, loaded on demand</dd>
        <dt>triggered</dt>
        <dd>
          Automatically when relevant, or with <code>/changelog</code>
        </dd>
        <dt>best for</dt>
        <dd>Repeatable workflows, formats and house rules</dd>
      </dl>
      <div class="kind-file">
        <div class="kind-file-path">
          <Icon name="file" />
          .claude/skills/changelog/SKILL.md
        </div>
        <pre><span class="d">---</span>
<span class="k">name</span>: changelog
<span class="k">description</span>: Writes a CHANGELOG.md entry from git…
<span class="k">allowed-tools</span>: Bash(git log:*) Read
<span class="d">---</span>

# Changelog
1. Find the range since the last release…</pre>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
